mits and pacing (Compaction), Connect a model provider, Give each agent its own model, the advisors file, the harness image, the settings reference, the glossary, Troubleshoot, the agents' explanation, campaign modes and the changelog. Left: the compose acceptances (claude, claude-real, codex, agents, steering) are to be run; Edit rig's info icon for OpenCode (`src/control/ui/edit-rig-client.ts`) still says "OpenCode does not report its compactions.", which is no longer so.
- 2026-10-21: In a run of the real-Claude acceptance, claude, codex and agents passed; claude-real failed only on its new compaction check (no compaction). The cause was in the check's stand-in model, not in Thermite: Claude Code 2.1.305 compacts at the owner's point through its "reactive" compaction, which summarizes only rounds before the newest one, and the stand-in reported the large conversation in the first round, so Claude Code bailed (see the decision above). The stand-in now makes two rounds, and the check runs Claude Code with its debug log on and, when it fails, prints the log's compaction lines, the hooks' folder and what the transcript shows. Limits and pacing says how Claude Code compacts a conversation still in its first round. The Edit rig text was changed with the merge.
- 2026-10-21: The next run of claude-real compacted, but the kept file was the conversation as Thermite saw it: the PreCompact hook had found no transcript. Claude Code 2.1.305 writes its transcript every 100 ms and runs the hook without writing first, so a real worker's copy would have lacked the newest lines (the last tool result, often), and the stand-in's quick rounds came before the first write. The hook now waits until the transcript has stopped growing (300 ms, 5 seconds at most) and records how long it waited; the check requires the last tool result in the kept file and prints the hook's records on a failure. claude-real then passed in full.
- 2026-10-22: Verified. Every box has its evidence. The acceptances passed with the kept conversation of all three CLI harnesses: claude, codex, agents, steering, rig-image, multi-GPU, smoke and control on 31d7efd; claude and steering again on bdc00ca; claude-real on 3d90e0c, where the real Claude Code 2.1.305 compacts a trial, its PreCompact hook keeps the whole transcript to the last tool result, and the summary names the kept file.

